    "notes": "Recorded from Claude Code 2.1.228 driving a disposable git repository under TMPDIR, never the AutoStack checkout. Machine-specific values are normalized to TRANSCRIPT_PLACEHOLDERS in both the frames and the recorded argv: the temp repository to /tmp/agent-workspace, the home directory to /home/agent, the username to agent. The `system/init` frame carries the operator's global hooks, plugins, skills, agents, slash commands and connected MCP servers, which are machine shape rather than protocol shape; those six keys are replaced by the values observed on the clean `--setting-sources project` re-run of the same session, and every other init field (session_id, uuid, cwd, model, permissionMode, claude_code_version) is the recording's own. `result` is a TURN boundary, not a session boundary: a steered session emits one `result` per turn, so `completed` must be minted on session end. This is the recorded steering session: with `--input-format stream-json` the process stays alive after a `result` frame and genuinely blocks on the open stdin until another user message arrives, which is what the `awaitStdin` frame represents -- the provider blocks rather than merely being slow. Two turns were driven in one session (APPLE, then a mid-session injection producing BANANA) under one session id, and Claude emits a fresh `system/init` frame at the start of each turn."
